From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:24:44 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Keep auto scroll to end across hiding and showing (runmanager
 #32)

set_auto_scroll_to_end recorded whether the scrollbar was at the end on every
valueChanged signal. Two changes that Qt makes itself cleared that record:

- When text is appended to a hidden QPlainTextEdit, Qt scrolls to the text
  cursor when the widget is next shown. If the user had clicked in the output
  box, the cursor was above the end, so the box scrolled up and stopped
  following new output.
- When a hidden QPlainTextEdit reaches its maximum block count, removing the
  first lines changes the scrollbar value without changing its maximum.

The scrollbar state is now recorded only while its scroll area is visible.
When the scroll area is shown, it is scrolled to the end after the show event
if it was at the end before. The two module-level dictionaries are replaced by
one dictionary of helper objects.

With an OutputBox in a tab widget, clicking in the box, switching to another
tab and writing 50 lines, then switching back, left the box scrolled to the
clicked line on PySide6 6.12, PyQt6 and PyQt5, and on Qt 6 it no longer
followed new output. With this change the box is at the end after switching
back and follows further output. A table view and a text edit that the user
scrolled up stay where the user left them.

